    "text": "Incident 2 is a platform scheduler failure (`platform_scheduler`, confidence 0.8). I recorded the diagnosis and proposed runbook steps for a person to follow. I changed nothing.\n\n- **What the health check saw:** the Airflow scheduler's last heartbeat was 214 s ago, against a 90 s limit. The incident has been open since 2026-11-02 19:25 UTC.\n- **What the cluster shows:** the `airflow-scheduler` Deployment was scaled from 1 to 0 at 2026-10-21 12:00 UTC, and its pod was stopped at the same time. No OOM kill, crash loop, or scheduling failure was recorded for the scheduler pod.\n- **What I could not check:** the Prometheus alert state was unavailable, so I could not confirm the firing alerts. I also did not look for a drill or change record that explains the scale-down.\n\nThe runbook (`09-scheduler-down`) says to scale the Deployment back to one replica. The proposed steps are:\n1. Confirm the Deployment is at 0 and no drill is running.\n2. Scale it to 1 with `kubectl -n dip-airflow scale deployment airflow-scheduler --replicas=1`.\n3. Confirm the heartbeat drops back under 90 s.\n4. Check for queued runs left over from the outage and confirm the incident closes.\n5. Find out who or what scaled it down on 2026-10-21. That date is about 12 days before the incident opened, so the gap needs explaining.",
